<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Steinhausen Pilgrimage Church</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1728">1728</a>–1733</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Wallfahrtskirche Steinhausen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The pilgrimage church at Steinhausen, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bad-schussenried">Bad Schussenried</a> in upper Swabia, was built from 1728 to 1733 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominikus-zimmermann">Dominikus Zimmermann</a> for the abbey of Schussenried, with frescoes by his brother Johann Baptist Zimmermann. Its oval plan and light-filled interior make it one of the first major works of the rococo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, and it is often called the most beautiful village church in the world.</p></div>
